# Contributing

Rocci is small enough that a focused change should remain easy to trace from
source syntax to generated Roc or HTML. Preserve that property when extending
the project.

## Set up the workspace

Follow [Installation](/getting-started/installation/), then run:

```sh
cargo test --workspace
```

Some end-to-end tests use Roc when it is available. Set
`ROCCI_REQUIRE_ROC=1` in CI lanes where skipping those tests would hide a
toolchain problem.

## Work in the owning layer

| Change | Primary owner |
| --- | --- |
| Template grammar or source maps | `rocci-template` |
| Markdown, Rocdown declarations, site catalog, and outputs | `rocci-rocdown` |
| CLI document and site commands | `rocci-rocdown-cli` |
| Runtime configuration | `rocci-core` |
| CLI template build, run, preview, or bundle behavior | `rocci-cli` and `rocci-wry` |
| Documentation site chrome | `crates/rocci-rocdown/templates/RocdownTheme.rocci` |

Do not interpret Rocci templates in Rust just to avoid compiling a theme. Do
not encode static documentation prose as Roc constructors just to keep catalog
logic in Roc.

## Inspect generated artifacts

For syntax work:

```sh
cargo run -p rocci-cli -- inspect --ast test/AllSyntax.rocci
cargo run -p rocci-cli -- inspect --ast test/AllSyntax.rocdown
```

For documentation work:

```sh
cargo run -p rocci-rocdown-cli -- build docs
```

Check generated HTML at narrow and wide widths, with keyboard navigation, in
light and dark color schemes, and with JavaScript disabled.

## Add tests at the right boundary

- Parser and lowering tests should run without spawning a server.
- Catalog and route tests should not require Roc.
- Theme application tests may require the pinned Roc toolchain.
- Runtime tests should exercise the same HTTP origin used by the webview.
- Failed static builds must preserve the previous output tree.

## Keep documentation current

When behavior changes, update the relevant Rocdown reference and the README in
the owning crate. Mark planned behavior as planned; do not present design-report
ideas as implemented features.
